NEWPAGE

 In your race's attempts to expand beyond the confines of your over-
 crowded world you have discovered that the rest of the galaxy is already 
 a very dark and uninviting place.

 The worlds of the sector are in a state of turmoil, cast into ever darkening
 wars that pit race against race. No longer is peaceful negotiation a pos-
 sible solution. As you realize that many races vie for the ultimate control 
 of the galaxy, you to are drawn into a wide-spread conflagration. If you do 
 not fight you will be destroyed.

 Once expansion seemed an easy enough task, now at least five other races
 also fight for control. Instead of the simple straight forward advance
 of your civilization now you must run the gauntlet that others have made
 for you...

                                            Leah Dahries
NEWPAGE

 This is a large, open-ended scenario for advanced players. Your goal is to
 conquer and prosper. Some of the other empires in the galaxy are easy prey,
 others are deadly predators. Though your initial resources are small, your
 skills and your experience will enable you to prevail.

ENDTEXT

BEGINDESCRIPTION

WorldBackgroundIndex
2:1 E:0		1	;Emp #1 Capital
2:2 E:1		2	;Troglidian Capital
2:8 E:2		3	;Paradine Capital
2:13 E:3	4	;Gaian Capital
2:18 E:4	5	;Egaly Capital
2:34 E:5	6	;Thinnva Capital
2:41 E:6	7	;Dakara Capital
2:46 E:7	8	;Soid Capital
EndIndex

TEXT 1
Algol, as the planet is known to the native inhabitants, is not the 
easiest planet in the galaxy to live on.  Life is difficult as the 
population soars to 50 billion, but the warriors of this planet, hardened
by the environment, are matched by none.

"Nothing stands in our way..."
ENDTEXT

TEXT 2
The capital of the Troglidian empire

A barren world to the naked eye, this planet hides thriving underground 
production factories.  The inhabitants of this world were quite advanced
before they ventured to the stars.  Hampered by a low population, 
efficiency is ingrained into their way of life.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 3
The capital of the Paradine empire, a lush and green world, is called a 
"Garden Paradise" by the inhabitants. As their age of star travel dawned,
the people of the world started a plan of colonization and conquest,
impatient for rapid expansion. Though they are the youngest of the space
faring empires, they have the potential to become an important power.         
ENDTEXT

TEXT 4
"Gaia", the capital of a strong and thriving empire, was once a world torn
by civil war. As soon as its inhabitants developed the ability to reach
the stars, they abandoned their planet-bound conflicts and united to forge
an interstellar empire. Although the old friction between internal factions
remain, the Gaians as a race tolerate no external interference.

It is said that before the collapse of the First Empire this world was
called "Earth" by its people, but there is no conclusive evidence to prove
that this world was indeed the mythical birthplace of humanity.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 5
The home world of the Egaly is a misty jungle world of fog and rainstorms.
Despite their fearsome looks, the Egaly are a very peaceful and intelligent
race. Their Kingdom was established long ago and has remained the same size
for centuries. Though harassed by the Thinnva, the empire is stable and 
productive.

Explorers that have been allowed to visit the Egaly empire say that most
of their ships are built by an ancient industrial complex.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 6
The Thinnva are tall and slender humanoids that have a very loose and
chaotic society. Often referred to as "parasites" by other races, the
Thinnva commonly attack transport fleets to steal their cargo. Though they
do not have many worlds, they are a most efficient and resourceful empire.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 7
This world of immense volcanic activity hides the race of the Dakara, a
violent people that dwell deep under the surface of their inhospitable
world.  The love of conquest and viciousness that these people demonstrate
is a constant surprise to other civilized races of the sector.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 8
The world of the Soid is a warm but stormy world, covered almost entirely
by ocean. The Soid, which can only be described as intelligent amorphous
blobs, live under the seas in great stone cities. Though little is actually
known about this race, their reputation for conquest is unquestionable.
So far, attempts to communicate with them have failed.
ENDTEXT

ENDDESCRIPTION

